<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO says van den Brink to join board.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO says van den Brink to join board.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Friday that Dolf van de Brink, senior executive vice-president of treasury and fixed income, would join its managing board.</p>
<p>It said van den Brink would succeed Ruud van Ommeren, who will leave the board after the annual meeting on May 7 on reaching retirement age.</p>
<p>He will also take over van Ommeren's responsibilities as chairman of the personnel and central services division and the information technology solutions division.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
